WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.464 --> 00:00:15.207
On their way home from church, Heidi and Grandfather passed Grannie's hut.

2
00:00:15.227 --> 00:00:19.571
"Please, let's stop for a visit," Heidi asked.

3
00:00:21.372 --> 00:00:27.858
Instead of finding a reason to stay outside as he usually did, Grandfather walked straight inside with Heidi

4
00:00:27.878 --> 00:00:32.532
and said, "Good afternoon, Grannie."

5
00:00:32.552 --> 00:00:35.973
"Dear God, if it isn't Grandfather!"

6
00:00:36.973 --> 00:00:38.834
Grannie cried in a pleased voice.

7
00:00:39.794 --> 00:00:43.655
Grannie and Grandfather had not spoken to each other for many years.

8
00:00:43.675 --> 00:00:47.956
"I never thought I would live to see such a day!

9
00:00:49.057 --> 00:00:50.937
May God reward you!"

10
00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:58.979
Heidi was very happy to see Grandfather so friendly with everyone and told Grannie all about the bells

11
00:00:59.139 --> 00:01:01.040
and church and visiting the pastor.

12
00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:05.808
Suddenly, gasping and breathless, Peter arrived at the hut.

13
00:01:07.389 --> 00:01:10.652
He was in such a hurry that he hit his head hard on the doorframe.

14
00:01:10.672 --> 00:01:17.738
"A letter, a letter," was all he could say, holding it out for everyone to see.

15
00:01:18.779 --> 00:01:21.201
No one there had ever received a letter before.

16
00:01:22.822 --> 00:01:25.845
The letter was addressed to Heidi and it was from Clara.

17
00:01:26.866 --> 00:01:32.445
Everyone sat down around the table and listened as Heidi read what Clara had to say.

18
00:01:34.065 --> 00:01:38.287
Dear Heidi, The house has been so dull since you left.

19
00:01:39.427 --> 00:01:42.828
I have persuaded my father to take me away in the autumn.

20
00:01:43.908 --> 00:01:49.150
Grandmamma is going to join us, and then, we will come to visit you on the mountain.

21
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:57.917
Grandmamma thinks that you made a very good decision taking the rolls to Grannie, but she does not

22
00:01:57.997 --> 00:02:00.539
like the idea of Grannie eating them dry.

23
00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.521
She is going to send some coffee.

24
00:02:04.582 --> 00:02:09.026
When we come, Grandmamma would like to meet Grandfather and Grannie both.

25
00:02:09.827 --> 00:02:10.607
Love, Clara.

26
00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:18.714
Everyone was astonished and pleased with the news, and they talked excitedly about the days to come.

27
00:02:19.714 --> 00:02:23.137
Finally, Heidi and Grandfather decided it was time to go.

28
00:02:24.859 --> 00:02:29.617
As the happy group separated, both Heidi and Grandfather promised to visit again soon.

29
00:02:29.637 --> 00:02:36.260
"I will patch some more holes in your hut before the autumn winds come," promised Grandfather.

30
00:02:38.281 --> 00:02:43.963
Unfortunately, just as Clara was excitedly preparing for her trip, her health turned for the worse.

31
00:02:44.943 --> 00:02:48.525
The doctor advised her father that Clara was too sick to travel.

32
00:02:49.485 --> 00:02:56.048
Herr Sesemann paced back and forth, scratching his chin as he always did when he was thinking hard.

33
00:02:57.672 --> 00:03:02.555
"My good friend, you shall go and visit Heidi on our behalf," he declared.

34
00:03:03.475 --> 00:03:07.077
The doctor was surprised; this was the furthest thing from his mind.

35
00:03:07.097 --> 00:03:11.800
"You have been sad ever since your daughter died," Herr Sesemann continued.

36
00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.221
"A journey is just the thing.

37
00:03:15.282 --> 00:03:18.364
And you can bring presents for Heidi from Clara and Grandmamma."

38
00:03:19.924 --> 00:03:23.987
Clara had been listening to the conversation with great disappointment up until now.

39
00:03:24.987 --> 00:03:27.520
She suddenly spoke up: "Oh, yes!

40
00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.082
You can see the mountain and meet Grandfather and Grannie and Peter and the goats.

41
00:03:34.222 --> 00:03:36.963
When you return, you can tell us all about them."

42
00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:42.405
When the doctor saw Clara smile, he knew that he couldn't disappoint her.

43
00:03:42.425 --> 00:03:44.985
"Yes, Clara," he said.

44
00:03:45.005 --> 00:03:48.807
"I will most certainly go and bring you back all the news I can.

45
00:03:49.687 --> 00:03:53.448
When I return, I expect that you will be well enough to go yourself!"

46
00:03:55.320 --> 00:04:00.591
Clara's father clapped his hands in approval and called for Sebastian and Fraulein to come join them.

47
00:04:01.472 --> 00:04:04.618
Soon, they were busily helping to plan the doctor's trip.
